// onsa.toml
// [test]
// mode = "none"
// spec = ["§2.4"]

// (R-01.) The forms of `\u{…}` (§2.4: the closed list ends with `\u{XXXX}`; a character is a Unicode scalar
// value): no digits, too many digits, a value past U+10FFFF, surrogates, an escape that is never
// closed, characters that are not hexadecimal digits, and the values at the edges of the scalar
// range that are fine. Whether seven or more digits with leading zeros are an escape is not in the
// spec, and the diagnostics of the cases that are decided are in
// tests/spec/negative/lex_utf8_escapes.onsa.

